REMARK   3                                                                      
REMARK   3 OTHER DETAILS: TO ADDRESS THE BREAKAGE OF SYMMETRY IN THE RING       
REMARK   3  -LIKE CORE REGION OF THE COMPLEX AND POSSIBLY REVOLVE THE MLEP-     
REMARK   3  RCRH2:MLEPTIN:MLEP-RCRH1-IGCRH2 SUBCOMPLEX AT HIGHER RESOLUTION,    
REMARK   3  THE PSEUDO-C3 SYMMETRIC VOLUME FOLLOWING CONSENUS REFINEMENT WAS    
REMARK   3  ALIGNED TO THE PSEUDO-C3 SYMMETRY AXIS VIA THE VOLUME ALIGNMENT     
REMARK   3  TOOL JOB IN CRYOSPARC. THE ASSOCIATED PARTICLE SET WAS RE-          
REMARK   3  EXTRACTED WITHOUT BINNING AND SYMMETRY EXPANDED AROUND THE C3       
REMARK   3  AXIS RESULTING IN 163,914 PARTICLES. USING THE MOLMAP FUNCTION      
REMARK   3  IN CHIMERA, A VOLUME BLURRED TO 25 ANGSTROM AROUND ONE MLEP-        
REMARK   3  RCRH2:MLEPTIN:MLEP-RCRH1-IGCRH2 SUBCOMPLEX WAS GENERATED, AND       
REMARK   3  TRANSFORMED INTO A MASK WITH THE VOLUME TOOLS JOB IN CRYOSPARC.     
REMARK   3  LOCAL REFINEMENT WAS PERFORMED BY LIMITING THE ROTATION AND         
REMARK   3  SHIFT SEARCH EXTENT AROUND THE ORIGINAL CONSENSUS REFINEMENT.       
REMARK   3  THE CENTER OF MASS OF THE MASK WAS USED AS A FULCRUM POINT. THIS    
REMARK   3  APPROACH RESULTED IN A CRYO-EM MAP WITH AN FSC0.143 RESOLUTION      
REMARK   3  OF 4.02 ANGSTROM IN WHICH THE CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC MODEL FOR THE        
REMARK   3  MLEP-RCRH2:MLEPTIN:MLEP-R_IGCRH2' COMPLEX WAS FITTED USING          
REMARK   3  CHIMERA AND REAL-SPACE REFINED IN PHENIX USING REFERENCE            
REMARK   3  RESTRAINTS TO THE STARTING MODEL.                                   
REMARK   4                                                                      
REMARK   4 8B7Q COMPLIES WITH FORMAT V. 3.30, 13-JUL-11                         
